<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#0d0a08">

  <title>
    {%- if page_title -%}
      {{ page_title }}{% unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless %}
    {%- else -%}
      {{ shop.name }}
    {%- endif -%}
  </title>

  {%- if page_description -%}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  <!-- Font preloads -->
  <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2"
    href="{{ 'cormorant-garamond-regular.woff2' | asset_url }}"
    crossorigin="anonymous">
  <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2"
    href="{{ 'barlow-condensed-regular.woff2' | asset_url }}"
    crossorigin="anonymous">

  <!-- Stylesheet -->
  {{ 'theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  <!-- Font faces -->
  {%- render 'font-faces' -%}

  {{ content_for_header }}

  {%- comment -%}
    Third-party IDs are resolved once here, and a value still carrying the word
    PLACEHOLDER is treated as unset.

    Every guard below tested `!= blank`, and a placeholder is not blank — it is
    a non-empty string that happens to be nonsense. So the live storefront was
    loading cdn.upromote.me/js/affiliate.min.js with
    data-merchant-id="UPROMOTE_MERCHANT_ID_PLACEHOLDER", and Klaviyo with a
    fake company_id, on every page view: two third-party requests that could
    never work, and an affiliate integration that looked wired up while
    tracking nothing.

    Same failure as the Cloudinary cloud name, which also shipped as
    "..._PLACEHOLDER" and passed a blank check. Worth remembering as a class:
    an unset credential should be empty, never a sentinel string, or every
    `!= blank` guard in the theme silently inverts.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign klaviyo_id = settings.klaviyo_company_id -%}
  {%- if klaviyo_id contains 'PLACEHOLDER' -%}{%- assign klaviyo_id = '' -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign ga4_id = settings.ga4_measurement_id -%}
  {%- if ga4_id contains 'PLACEHOLDER' -%}{%- assign ga4_id = '' -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign upromote_id = settings.upromote_merchant_id -%}
  {%- if upromote_id contains 'PLACEHOLDER' -%}{%- assign upromote_id = '' -%}{%- endif -%}

  {%- if klaviyo_id != blank -%}
    <script async type="text/javascript"
      src="https://static.klaviyo.com/onsite/js/klaviyo.js?company_id={{ klaviyo_id }}">
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if ga4_id != blank -%}
    <script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id={{ ga4_id }}"></script>
    <script>
      window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
      function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
      gtag('js', new Date());
      gtag('config', '{{ ga4_id }}', { send_page_view: true });
    </script>

    <script id="ga4-page-data" type="application/json">
      {
        "pageType": {{ request.page_type | json }},
        "currency": "USD"
        {%- if product -%}
        ,"product": {
          "id": {{ product.id | json }},
          "name": {{ product.title | json }},
          "brand": {{ shop.name | json }},
          "category": {{ product.type | json }},
          "variant": {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | json }},
          "price": {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | money_without_currency | json }},
          "sku": {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku | json }},
          "imageUrl": {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 600 | json }}
        }
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if collection -%}
        ,"collection": {
          "id": {{ collection.id | json }},
          "name": {{ collection.title | json }},
          "products": [
            {%- for p in collection.products limit: 50 -%}
              {
                "id": {{ p.id | json }},
                "name": {{ p.title | json }},
                "price": {{ p.price | money_without_currency | json }},
                "position": {{ forloop.index }},
                "category": {{ p.type | json }}
              }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          ]
        }
        {%- endif -%}
      }
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if upromote_id != blank -%}
    <script async
      src="https://cdn.upromote.me/js/affiliate.min.js"
      data-merchant-id="{{ upromote_id | escape }}">
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}
</head>

<body
  class="bg-cream text-deep font-body pt-16"
  data-customer-email="{{ customer.email | escape }}"
  data-customer-id="{{ customer.id }}"
  data-klaviyo-company-id="{{ klaviyo_id | escape }}"
  data-ga4-id="{{ ga4_id | escape }}"
>
  <!-- Custom cursor (hidden on touch devices) -->
  <div id="custom-cursor"
    class="pointer-events-none fixed top-0 left-0 z-[9999] w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-coral mix-blend-difference will-change-transform hidden md:block"
    aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <a href="#main-content" class="sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:top-4 focus:left-4 bg-deep text-cream px-4 py-2 z-50">
    Skip to content
  </a>

  {% section 'announcement-bar' %}
  {% section 'header' %}
  {% section 'cart-drawer' %}

  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    {{ content_for_layout }}
  </main>

  {% section 'footer' %}

  <script type="module" src="{{ 'custom-cursor.js' | asset_url }}"></script>

  {%- if klaviyo_id != blank -%}
    <script type="module" src="{{ 'klaviyo.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Referral capture is deliberately NOT gated on the UpPromote merchant ID.

    ref-capture.js reads ?ref=CODE and upromote.js appends it to checkout links
    as ?discount=CODE. That is plain Shopify discounting — it needs a discount
    code to exist, not an app. Gating it on the merchant ID meant that with no
    UpPromote account the referral links did nothing at all, when they could
    have been carrying attribution the moment a code was created.

    Both are inert without a ?ref= in the URL: getInfluencerCode() returns null
    and upromote.js returns early before touching the DOM.

    Only the vendor script above is gated, because that one genuinely needs a
    real merchant ID.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script type="module" src="{{ 'ref-capture.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
  <script type="module" src="{{ 'upromote.js' | asset_url }}"></script>

  {%- if ga4_id != blank -%}
    <script type="module" src="{{ 'ga4.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
  {%- endif -%}

  {% section 'cookie-consent' %}
</body>
</html>
